WEBVTT

00:30.000 --> 00:37.000
Ilyon represents the union of the heart and body, which is the mind and matter respectively.

00:37.000 --> 00:44.000
The progress line of Ilyopumse is the character Ma, which means fill fat,

00:44.000 --> 00:49.000
and is composed of moves to cultivate isometry and equilibrium.

00:50.000 --> 00:54.000
We will now take a look at the key moves of Ilyopumse.

01:30.000 --> 01:32.000
Ilyopumse

02:00.000 --> 02:05.000
Ilyopumse

02:09.000 --> 02:17.000
Ilyopumse consists of four key moves, namely, isometry and equilibrium,

02:17.000 --> 02:25.000
face-to-face, and two-handed push-and-pull,

02:26.000 --> 02:28.000
two-handed push-and-pull,

02:29.000 --> 02:31.000
and two-handed push-and-pull.

02:35.000 --> 02:40.000
We will now take a closer look at each of the key moves of Ilyopumse.

02:40.000 --> 02:46.000
Weisanteu-yopchagi is a technique to cross the two arms in front of the chest

02:46.000 --> 02:53.000
and slowly perform anpalmok-bakkatmakgi and mejumok-bakkatjigi simultaneously.

02:53.000 --> 02:57.000
Both hands and arms must move in unison.

02:59.000 --> 03:04.000
Okkoro-olgomakki is a move to raise the arms from the right back,

03:04.000 --> 03:07.000
then block by diagonally crossing both arms.

03:07.000 --> 03:11.000
Both wrists should cross in front of the forehead.

03:13.000 --> 03:16.000
When blocking, place your left hand outside

03:16.000 --> 03:19.000
and use your right hand to cross your wrists diagonally.

03:20.000 --> 03:23.000
Open the hands and twist your right hand inward,

03:23.000 --> 03:28.000
your left hand outward so the bottom part of your wrists touch each other,

03:28.000 --> 03:32.000
to pull an opponent's wrist and thrust or twist their wrist.

03:35.000 --> 03:40.000
When performing tuyo-yopchagi, stamp the ground with the front kicking leg,

03:40.000 --> 03:45.000
then pull the opposite knee upward to jump and kick sideways.

03:45.000 --> 03:49.000
Pull the back of the opposite foot blade on the inside of the kicking leg,

03:49.000 --> 03:53.000
then bend your knee and land after the kick.

03:53.000 --> 03:58.000
Be careful not to perform the kick after the body has already twisted.

03:59.000 --> 04:04.000
Oglomsogi is a posture to stand by placing the back of the foot blade

04:04.000 --> 04:07.000
in the crook behind the supporting knee.

04:08.000 --> 04:10.000
The knees should face forward.

04:11.000 --> 04:15.000
These are the four key moves of Ilyopumse.

04:16.000 --> 04:21.000
We will now look at the moves in succession, connecting each move.

04:24.000 --> 04:28.000
The key moves of Ilyo first part consist of

04:28.000 --> 04:35.000
Wensonna Kodoromaki, Orenjiriki, Kumgangmaki,

04:35.000 --> 04:42.000
and Wensonna Kodoromaki, Orenjiriki, and Wensonna Sewojiriki.

04:43.000 --> 04:51.000
Wensonna Kodoromaki, Orenjiriki, and Wensonna Sewojiriki.

04:52.000 --> 04:59.000
When connecting from Wensonna Kodoromaki to Jiriki during Ilyo first part,

05:00.000 --> 05:06.000
pull the fist of the assisting arm to the back, then perform Jiriki.

05:07.000 --> 05:12.000
Perform Kumgangmaki slowly, exerting force on the lower abdomen.

05:12.000 --> 05:14.000
Run and set with the right foot.

05:14.000 --> 05:17.000
The right foot should set first and touch the ground.

05:17.000 --> 05:23.000
Then, complete Pyeonseongkut Sewojiriki the moment the back of the left foot blade

05:23.000 --> 05:26.000
touches the crook behind the right knee.

05:27.000 --> 05:32.000
The back of the hind foot blade stops momentum by touching the crook

05:32.000 --> 05:35.000
and transfers the force to the tip of the hands.

05:38.000 --> 05:41.000
We will now connect these moves in succession.

05:57.000 --> 06:04.000
The key moves of Ilyo second part consist of

06:04.000 --> 06:11.000
Wensonna Kodoromaki, Orenjiriki, Kumgangmaki,

06:17.000 --> 06:24.000
Wensonna Kodoromaki, Orenjiriki, and Orenpyeonseongkut Sewojiriki.

06:25.000 --> 06:30.000
When Wensanto Yeopjagi starts with both arms crossing in front of the chest

06:30.000 --> 06:33.000
in the Ogunseogi posture,

06:33.000 --> 06:38.000
your left and right arms are crossed from the inside and outside respectively.

06:38.000 --> 06:41.000
Your right arm performs Olgulbakkadmaki.

06:41.000 --> 06:46.000
The left arm draws a circle outward, like you're performing Mejumokbakkadchigi.

06:46.000 --> 06:51.000
Then, perform Yeopjagi with the left leg and arm positioned parallel.

06:51.000 --> 06:58.000
When performing Okuro Olgumaki, cross both arms diagonally from the right back and block upward.

06:58.000 --> 07:04.000
Cross the arms diagonally and block upward with the right arm on top of the left arm.

07:04.000 --> 07:08.000
When blocking, the wrists should be crossed diagonally

07:08.000 --> 07:13.000
with the left arm on the outside and right arm on the inside.

07:13.000 --> 07:15.000
Open your hands.

07:15.000 --> 07:19.000
Twist your right hand inward and your left hand outward

07:19.000 --> 07:23.000
so the bottom part of your wrists touch each other.

07:23.000 --> 07:28.000
Then, pull and thrust or twist an opponent's wrist.

07:31.000 --> 07:35.000
Pull the assisting fist to the back during Wensonna Kodoromaki,

07:35.000 --> 07:39.000
then connect to Jiriki.

07:39.000 --> 07:41.000
Run and set with the right foot,

07:41.000 --> 07:45.000
and when performing Kodoro Orenpyeonseongkut Sewojiriki,

07:45.000 --> 07:48.000
the right foot should set first and touch the ground.

07:48.000 --> 07:51.000
Then, complete Pyeonseongkut Sewojiriki

07:51.000 --> 07:57.000
the moment the back of the left foot blade touches the crook behind the knee.

07:57.000 --> 08:02.000
Cautions for Ilyo 2nd part, taking a closer look.

08:02.000 --> 08:07.000
The tip of the open hand used during Kodoro Pyeonseongkut Sewojiriki

08:07.000 --> 08:13.000
is the left for Ilyo 1st part and the right for Ilyo 2nd part.

08:14.000 --> 08:19.000
Remember that all moves of Ilyo Pumse must naturally connect.

08:21.000 --> 08:27.000
We will now practice the moves of Ilyo 2nd part in succession while watching the video.

08:44.000 --> 08:49.000
The key moves of Ilyo 3rd part consist of

08:49.000 --> 09:05.000
Wen Wesantuyopchagi, Okkoro Olgulmakki, Orenjiriki, Kumgangmakki, and Ddujumokhwari.

09:05.000 --> 09:11.000
Some of the moves from Ilyo 2nd part are repeated in Ilyo 3rd part.

09:11.000 --> 09:18.000
Be mindful of the previous explanations and practice the Wesantuyopchagi again.

09:18.000 --> 09:23.000
Start with the arm crossing in front of the chest at the Ogeumseogi posture.

09:23.000 --> 09:29.000
Your left and right arms are crossed from the inside and outside respectively.

09:29.000 --> 09:32.000
Your right arm performs Olgulbakkakmakki.

09:32.000 --> 09:39.000
Your left arm draws a circle outward as if to perform Mejumokbakkachigi.

09:39.000 --> 09:44.000
Then perform Yopchagi with the left leg and arm parallel.

09:44.000 --> 09:50.000
The following move is also performed as explained in Ilyo 2nd part.

09:50.000 --> 09:57.000
When performing Okkoro Olgulmakki, cross both arms diagonally from right back and block upward.

09:57.000 --> 10:01.000
Cross the wrists diagonally in front of the forehead.

10:01.000 --> 10:07.000
When blocking, cross the wrists with the left arm outside and the right arm inside.

10:07.000 --> 10:12.000
Just like Duseonpyo Bituro Chapa Dangigi.

10:12.000 --> 10:17.000
Open the hands and twist your right hand inward and your left hand outward

10:17.000 --> 10:20.000
so the bottom part of your wrist touch each other

10:20.000 --> 10:25.000
to pull an opponent's wrist and thrust or twist their wrist.

10:25.000 --> 10:31.000
When performing Ddujumokhwari, move your center with your right foot.

10:32.000 --> 10:38.000
Then turn 90 degrees to the left using the right ball of your foot as an axis.

10:38.000 --> 10:46.000
Next, slowly straighten the body and pull the fists next to the back on both sides.

10:49.000 --> 10:54.000
Cautions for Ilyo 3rd part, taking a closer look.

10:54.000 --> 10:57.000
When assuming the Ddujumokhwari posture,

10:57.000 --> 11:04.000
be careful not to cross the arms or perform the move after straightening the arm forward.

11:06.000 --> 11:12.000
We will now practice the moves of Ilyo 3rd part in succession while watching the video.

11:28.000 --> 11:32.000
The key moves of Ilyo 4th part consist of

11:32.000 --> 12:00.000
Ilyo 4th part starts from the last move of Ilyo 3rd part.

12:00.000 --> 12:04.000
The Ddujumokhwari posture with the feet gathered together.

12:04.000 --> 12:08.000
Perform Orun Aptagi from this position.

12:08.000 --> 12:14.000
Be careful not to lift the left heel when kicking.

12:14.000 --> 12:19.000
We will now watch the connection from the previous Ddujumokhwari posture

12:19.000 --> 12:24.000
to the first move of Ilyo 4th part.

12:25.000 --> 12:34.000
After completing the Orun Aptagi, connect to the Wen Dduyeol Yeoptagi.

12:34.000 --> 12:41.000
Lift your body by pulling your left knee above your back the moment your foot touches the ground.

12:41.000 --> 12:46.000
Gather your feet, then perform Dduyeol Yeoptagi with your left foot.

12:46.000 --> 12:51.000
Pull the right leg toward the left knee and let it touch.

12:55.000 --> 13:01.000
Afterwards, Okkoro Olgulmakgi and Ddusompyo Ppittoro Jabattanggigi.

13:01.000 --> 13:08.000
The key moves of Ilyo are repeated once more.

13:08.000 --> 13:15.000
Perform these moves remembering what we learned earlier.

13:15.000 --> 13:21.000
Then perform Kumgangmakgi again, slowly exerting some force into it.

13:21.000 --> 13:25.000
Next, move your center to your right foot.

13:25.000 --> 13:31.000
Turn 90 degrees to the left using your right ball as an axis.

13:31.000 --> 13:36.000
Slowly straighten your body, pull your fists to the back on both sides,

13:36.000 --> 13:40.000
and connect to Ddujumokhwari posture.

13:40.000 --> 13:43.000
Continue with Wen Aptagi.

13:43.000 --> 13:50.000
Lift your body by pulling your right knee above your back the moment your left foot touches the ground.

13:50.000 --> 13:56.000
Gather your feet, then perform Dduyeol Yeoptagi with your right foot.

13:56.000 --> 14:04.000
As with Wen Dduyeol Yeoptagi, pull the left leg toward the right knee and let it touch.

14:04.000 --> 14:09.000
Cautions for Ilyo 4th part, taking a closer look.

14:09.000 --> 14:15.000
When assuming the Ddujumokhwari posture, be careful not to cross the arms,

14:15.000 --> 14:19.000
or perform the move after straightening the arm forward.

14:19.000 --> 14:27.000
When performing Okkoromakki, remember that the arm on the side of the set foot must be on the outside.

14:29.000 --> 14:35.000
We will now practice the moves of Ilyo 4th part in succession while watching the video.

14:49.000 --> 14:52.000
This concludes the training for Ilyo Pumse.

14:52.000 --> 14:57.000
We will take another look at all the moves and master Pumse.

15:19.000 --> 15:21.000
Ilyo 4th part

15:49.000 --> 15:51.000
Ilyo 4th part

16:20.000 --> 16:29.000
We have looked at the key moves of Ilyo Pumse and provided thorough explanations for each move and things to watch out for.

16:29.000 --> 16:37.000
You did a fine job reaching the last section of the Pumse, the last stage of Taekwondo training.

16:37.000 --> 16:42.000
Cherish the feeling of this moment and continue with your training.

16:42.000 --> 16:47.000
You will learn to be able to perfect all the postures and moves.

16:47.000 --> 16:51.000
We again commend you for a job well done.

